  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 3226.05 Wheel Pulling Not Required on Some Vehicles",
  "priorExpiration": "2016-01-12",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3226.05 Wheel Pulling Not Required on Some Vehicles. If a truck or bus is equipped with an inspection port or dust shield which can be removed to determine the condition of the drum and the brake-block thickness, the mechanic shall not be required to pull a wheel, but brakes on all the wheels shall be visually inspected through the inspection ports.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes at Chapter Heading Saf-C 3200) #8915, eff 6-22-07, EXPIRED: 6-22-15\n\nNew. #10886, INTERIM, eff 7-16-15, EXPIRES: 1-12-16; ss by #11016, eff 1-6-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3200.html"
